> Hand-check the residual, shared RGB noise and amplitude

For p=2 and residual logit(-1,0,1), adding tanh gives approximately
(1.2384,2,2.7616): a bounded correction does not clamp the previous image.
The derivative with respect to p includes the identity skip as well as the
convolution path. At zero amplitude the image cannot depend on the supplied noise.

Source coarse noise draws one Gaussian value per pixel and repeats it across
RGB. Finer noise draws all RGB coordinates in one contiguous stream. The native
sampler uses local raw MT19937 words with midpoint uniforms and Box-Muller,
then casts once to Float32. It never consumes a global RNG stream.

Higher-scale amplitudes are measured once from the frozen fixed reconstruction:

$$ a_k=.1\sqrt{\frac{\sum_i(\operatorname{Double}(p_i^{rec})-
\operatorname{Double}(x_{k,i}))^2}{NHW3}},\qquad a_0=1. $$
\alttext(Higher-scale amplitude is one tenth of root mean square reconstruction error, using Double differences and one final Float32 cast; the coarse amplitude is one.)

The measurement stops both image gradients and returns[1], preserving the source
scalar convention. The generator separately accepts a live scalar or[1]
amplitude, so callers may differentiate an explicitly supplied amplitude.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/sig_residual_toy.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n=dm::nn; auto t=n::DType::Float64;
  auto p=n::full({3},2,t), residual=n::tanh(n::tensor({-1.,0.,1.},{3},t));
  auto image=p+residual;
  auto coarse=n::models::SingleImageNoise(1,1,2,true,7411);
  auto a=n::models::SingleImageAmplitude(n::ones({1,2,3,3}),n::zeros({1,2,3,3}));
  if(a.requires_grad() || std::abs(a.item()-.1)>1e-8) throw std::runtime_error("RMS amplitude");
  auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  plot.lines({0,1,2},p.to_vector<double>(),"Previous",{37,99,235})
      .lines({0,1,2},image.to_vector<double>(),"Add tanh",{220,38,38})
      .points({0,1,2},residual.to_vector<double>(),"Correction",{22,163,74},5)
      .y_limits(-1.1,3.6).x_label("Supplied residual logits -1, 0, 1")
      .y_label("Signed value").title("A bounded correction leaves the image unbounded")
      .save_svg("build/sig_residual_toy.svg");
  std::print("Shared RGB bank: {}\nDetached RMS amplitude: {}\n",coarse.values_str(),a.item());
}
