> Keep the loss factors and both generator branches explicit

Let R=D(x), F=D(G(p,z,a)) and q=G(p_rec,z_rec,a). Each score pool has its own
mean; random and real row counts may differ. The source game is

$$ L_D=\tfrac12[\operatorname{mean}(R-1)^2+\operatorname{mean}F^2],\quad
L_G=\operatorname{mean}(F-1)^2+10\operatorname{mean}(q-x)^2. $$
\alttext(Discriminator loss is half the sum of real-to-one and fake-to-zero squared means. Generator loss is the full fake-to-one squared mean plus ten times reconstruction MSE.)

Both G calls share all weights. D receives only an image, not a target, noise or
amplitude. There is no half on G's adversarial term. Thus dL_D/dF_j=F_j/M,
while the adversarial dL_G/dF_j=2(F_j-1)/M. Reconstruction contributes
20(q_i-x_i)/(N_real*H*W*3) through the second use of G. Its lower reconstruction
is frozen; the current generator remains differentiable on both branches.
With R=(0,2), F=(-1,1), and residual reconstruction errors(2,-2), D=1 and G=42.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/sig_loss_toy.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n=dm::nn; auto t=n::DType::Float64;
  auto r=n::tensor({0.,2.},{2},t), f=n::tensor({-1.,1.},{2},t).requires_grad_();
  auto e=n::tensor({2.,-2.},{2},t);
  auto d=.5*(n::mean(n::square(r-1))+n::mean(n::square(f)));
  auto g=n::mean(n::square(f-1))+10*n::mean(n::square(e));
  n::GradOptions keep;keep.retain_graph=true;
  auto dd=n::grad(d,{f},keep)[0],gg=n::grad(g,{f})[0];
  if(d.item()!=1 || g.item()!=42) throw std::runtime_error("loss factors");
  auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  plot.points({-1,1},dd.to_vector<double>(),"D partial",{37,99,235},6)
      .points({-1,1},gg.to_vector<double>(),"G partial",{220,38,38},6)
      .y_limits(-2.4,1.5).x_label("Supplied fake patch score")
      .y_label("Partial with respect to fake score").title("Half D and full G have different score partials")
      .save_svg("build/sig_loss_toy.svg");
  std::print("| Supplied scores | D | G including reconstruction |\n|---|---|---|\n| R=(0,2), F=(-1,1) | {} | {} |\n",d.item(),g.item());
}
