> Remove one noise level at a time and check the limits

For each control, preserve the other two noise banks and all weights, but set one
scale's random noise to zero. Each level changes the final raw RGB samples.
That establishes an active path, not semantic diversity or perceptual quality.
The sample pixel variance.006276 is the average squared difference from the
12-sample per-coordinate mean. It is neither a distribution metric nor an
accuracy measure. Reconstruction MSE.1290 is on the sole training image.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/sig_noise_controls.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n=dm::nn;std::map<std::string,n::Tensor> controls,samples;
  for(auto& [key,value]:n::load_npz("build/singan/noise_controls.npz"))controls.emplace(key,value);
  for(auto& [key,value]:n::load_npz("build/singan/samples.npz"))samples.emplace(key,value);
  std::vector<double> rms,maximum;
  for(int k=0;k<3;++k){
    auto delta=n::cast(controls.at("zero_noise_scale"+std::to_string(k)),n::DType::Float64)-n::cast(samples.at("scale2_fake"),n::DType::Float64);
    rms.push_back(n::sqrt(n::mean(n::square(delta))).item());maximum.push_back(n::max(n::abs(delta)).item());
    if(maximum.back()<=1e-7)throw std::runtime_error("inactive noise control");
  }
  auto p=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  p.points({0,1,2},rms,"RMS change",{37,99,235},6).points({0,1,2},maximum,"Max change",{220,38,38},6)
   .y_limits(0,1.5).x_label("Only this scale receives zero noise").y_label("Change in final raw RGB")
   .title("All three noise levels affect the final image").save_svg("build/sig_noise_controls.svg");
  std::print("| Zero noise at scale | RMS change | Maximum change |\n|---|---|---|\n");
  for(int k=0;k<3;++k)std::print("| {} | {} | {} |\n",k,rms[k],maximum[k]);
}
```
